# Architecture

Follow [architecture.md](architecture.md). It is the decision record. [initial_idea.md](initial_idea.md) is the proposal.

When a decision changes, edit architecture.md in the same change. That includes boundaries, resolution, hardware that is in or out, engine flags, folder layout, a memory-slice size, or a new resident in the memory table.

- Game code is C. SoA, free functions, fixed capacity. No classes, templates, exceptions, RTTI, or STL containers in `game/`.
- C++ we write stays in the engine host and the ST7789 drawer, because PixelRoot32's API is C++. Patches inside the vendored engine stay in that tree.
- `game/` does not include PixelRoot32 or ESP-IDF, and does not call `malloc` or `free`.
- `third_party/pixelroot32` and `third_party/pixelroot32-apu` are vendored snapshots and may be patched. Board pins and the panel stay in the drawer.
- Bluetooth LE stays on in the device build. Wi-Fi stays off. The PC pad reader stays out of the device sources.
